THIRD-PARTY LICENSES
====================

Every crate linked into the WeftDB binaries — `weft-server`, `weft-tui` and
`weft-bench` — is listed below with the license text that covers it, grouped by
license. This file is generated: do not edit it by hand.

	generated by:  scripts/licenses/generate.sh
	checked by:    the `third-party licenses` job of .github/workflows/ci.yml
	scope:         the five targets .github/workflows/release.yml builds, unioned,
	               so the Windows-only and macOS-only crates are named too
	excluded:      dev-dependencies, which never link into a released binary.
	               Build dependencies are included: a `-sys` build script links
	               foreign code into the archive.

WeftDB's own code is MIT OR Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE). The
notices for the third-party source WeftDB adapts — Chimp and DDSketch — are not
dependency licenses, so they are not listed here; they ship in the same archive
as `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES-weft-physical-type` and
`THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES-weft-reduce`.

A crate that publishes more than one license text is listed once per text, with
the crates that use that exact text above it, so the attribution lines stay with
the license they belong to.

The WeftDB crates appear in the list too, where one workspace crate depends on
another. Their texts are the ones at the root of the repository: `LICENSE-MIT`
and `LICENSE-APACHE` are picked up from the checkout, which is why they are here
rather than assumed.

